    {
      "id": 22,
      "code": "G",
      "title": "should / shouldn't",
      "rule": "*should* — maslahat berishda ishlatiladi: \"…ishingiz kerak, …sangiz yaxshi boʻladi\". Hamma shaxs uchun bir xil, keyin feʼlning asosiy shakli keladi (*to* siz, *-s* siz): *You should sleep. He should study.* Inkor: *shouldn't* (= *should not*): *You shouldn't eat a lot of sugar.* Soʻroq: *Should I go to the doctor?* — *should* egadan oldin turadi.",
      "examples": [
        "You should drink some water.",
        "Bekzod should study every day.",
        "You shouldn't eat a lot of sugar.",
        "Aziz shouldn't go to bed late.",
        "Should I go to the doctor?",
        "We should visit Hamida."
      ],
      "words": [
        { "en": "should", "uz": "…ishi kerak (maslahat)" },
        { "en": "shouldn't", "uz": "…masligi kerak" },
        { "en": "doctor", "uz": "shifokor" },
        { "en": "medicine", "uz": "dori" },
        { "en": "ill", "uz": "kasal" },
        { "en": "go to bed", "uz": "uxlashga yotmoq" },
        { "en": "stay at home", "uz": "uyda qolmoq" },
        { "en": "rest", "uz": "dam olmoq" }
      ],
      "text": {
        "title": "Bekzod is ill",
        "en": "Bekzod is ill today. He has got a cold. Nodira is a nurse. She says: You should stay at home. You should drink hot tea. You shouldn't go to school today. You should sleep a lot. Bekzod asks: Should I take some medicine? Nodira says: Yes, you should. And you shouldn't play football this week."
      },
